WEBVTT

NOTE Culla demo video (en). Source: docs/videos.md (a), shot list. 82.7 s.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.900
After a shoot, you come home with hundreds
of photos, each a JPEG and a RAW.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.800
Sorting them by hand is slow,
and the RAW is easy to leave behind.

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.800
As you sort, Culla shows
where every photo will go:

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.800
keepers to your folder, rejects set aside,
the rest left alone.

5
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.000
Then look at each photo once,
and keep it or reject it.

6
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.800
Each decision takes one click.

7
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.800
Or use the arrow keys:
right to keep, left to reject.

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.800
Under each button, Culla shows
where this photo would go.

9
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.600
Changed your mind? Ctrl+Z walks
back through your decisions.

10
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.800
Nothing has moved yet.

11
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
When you're done, review the whole plan:
what is kept, what is rejected,

12
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.800
and every file it will move.

13
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.800
Only then does anything happen.

14
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.400
Keepers go to your folder,
rejects go to a _rejected folder.

15
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.600
Nothing is deleted.

16
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.600
Nothing is overwritten or deleted.

17
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.600
Every apply can resume after a crash.

18
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.600
Culla, for Windows 11.
